     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the dose looks like a possible error, and I'd like you to confirm it first.\n\n**The problem:** 1700 mg three times daily comes to **5100 mg per day**. That's double the labeled maximum for immediate-release metformin (2550 mg/day) and well over the maximum for extended-release (2000 mg/day). Doses that high raise the risk of severe GI side effects and lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\n**Possible intended orders:**\n- **850 mg by mouth three times daily with meals** (2550 mg/day, the IR maximum). The 1700 may have come from the twice-daily regimen.\n- **1700 mg per day total**, for example 850 mg twice daily.\n- **Something else**, such as a different strength or formulation (IR vs. ER).\n\nTell me which dose you meant and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1700 mg three times daily, confirm that and give a short reason, and I'll enter it with a note documenting the dose above the labeled maximum and your confirmation."
      }
     ],
