       "type": "text",
       "text": "I entered the order as written. It's **ORD-0001: metformin 1700 mg by mouth, three times daily with meals.**\n\nThe order carries a note saying the total of 5100 mg/day is above the labeled maximum, that you confirmed the dose as written, and that no clinical reason was given. It also asks for pharmacist verification, so pharmacy will probably contact you before dispensing.\n\nTwo things worth doing:\n- **Add a short reason to the chart** for the high dose. That will make pharmacy review faster.\n- **If this patient continues on this dose,** watch for GI side effects and signs of lactic acidosis, such as malaise, muscle pain, trouble breathing or abdominal pain. Checking lactate and kidney function would be reasonable, and so would stopping the drug before IV contrast or if the patient becomes acutely unwell.\n\nIf you meant 850 mg three times daily after all, let me know and I'll help correct the order."
      }
